  "id": "gr-to-and",
  "connector": "と",
  "gloss": "and; with",
  "title": "と — and, with",
  "pattern": "A と B / person と verb",
  "explanation": "と joins nouns into a list: パンと{卵|たまご} — bread and eggs. It also means “with” someone: {友達|ともだち}と{映画|えいが}を{見|み}ます — I’m watching a film with a friend. It only joins nouns, never whole sentences.",
  "natural": "For a list that goes on (“…and so on”), use や: パンや{卵|たまご} — bread, eggs and the like.",
  "stiff": "To join actions, と is wrong: use the て form (a Basic lesson). {食|た}べて{寝|ね}る is “eat and sleep”; {食|た}べると{寝|ね}る means “whenever I eat, I sleep”.",
